  "note": "CLAIM_CONFORMANCE checks against the simulated agent lane over the in-process loopback facade (CapitalService). Results are SIMULATED. The lane is a Capital fixture (SIMULATED_AGENT_GRANT / IN_MEMORY_FIXTURE), not the upstream reference/ai_delegation/ai_delegation_mock.py, which stays a read-only reference and is not vendored. Adapter mapping, stated honestly: the draft's PROPOSED memo phase maps to the lane's HUMAN_PENDING label; the draft's always-failing attempt_execution (DELEGATED_EXECUTION_DISABLED) maps to the lane's EXECUTE_AUTHORITY_DISABLED refusal; the draft's PROPOSED/HUMAN_APPROVED decision flow has no lane counterpart because the lane has no decide step — a human organizer command may cite a pending proposal_id on its receipt without executing the memo. Money and two-person values come from the adopted CAPITAL-TERMS-V1 underwriting_depth entry, not from the draft, which leaves product limits undetermined. A missing protocol checkout is SKIPPED and is not a pass.",
